==> final_solution/code/README.md <==
# OpenVaccine (MCRMSE) — swarm solution code

Task: predict per-position degradation rates for 107-nt mRNA sequences.
Scored columns: `reactivity`, `deg_Mg_pH10`, `deg_Mg_50C` (positions 0..67). Metric: **MCRMSE** (lower is better).

## Validation protocol
Canonical 5-fold `KFold(n_splits=5, shuffle=True, random_state=42)` over the 2160 train rows.
All model selection / early stopping on validation rows with `SN_filter==1` (test is SN-filtered).
Reported metric = MCRMSE over the 3 scored cols on `SN_filter==1` rows.

## Model families (all trained only on `data/train.json`)
1. `train_nn.py` — CNN stem + BiGRU/BiLSTM, loss on 3 scored cols only, sample weight = `signal_to_noise`.
2. `train_ms.py` — multi-scale Conv1d (k=3/5/9) → BiGRU-512, same loss/weighting.
3. `train_struct2.py` — **structure-aware**: 3-channel base-pair contact tensor (binary contact / pair type / pair distance) → 2D CNN → row-pooled partner context, concatenated with multi-scale 1D conv → BiGRU-512, same loss/weighting. Best single model (5-fold sn1 CV 0.22002).

`train_struct3.py` additionally appends per-position partner base/loop-type channels.

## Post-processing / ensembling (`ensemble.py`)
- Per scored column, non-negative least squares (ridge-augmented NNLS) over all model OOF predictions, fit on `SN_filter==1` rows.
- kNN correction (`knn_final.py`): similarity = 0.7·identity(first 68 nt) + 0.3·identity(full 107), k=5, weight=sim^4.
  Gated blend `p = (1-w)·NNLS + w·kNN`, `w = clip((sim_max-0.8)/0.2,0,1)·0.3`; then clip predictions at 0.
  (Split-half validated: gain +0.0028, positive 30/30.)
- `make_submission.py` writes `id_seqpos,reactivity,deg_Mg_pH10,deg_pH10,deg_Mg_50C,deg_50C` for all 240×107 positions.

